Description:

Setting the "shareWith" property of a JMAP Mailbox now requires administrative
access to that mailbox.  Previously, the nonstandard mailbox sharing feature of
JMAP for Mail let any user with whom a mailbox had been shared change the
permissions on it, including granting themselves or others further access.

Creating a mailbox with "shareWith" now likewise requires administrative access
to the parent mailbox, matching the behavior of the JMAP calendar and
addressbook sharing handlers.


CVE number: CVE-2026-111859


CVE description:

Changing mailbox permissions gated by wrong permissions

Through the nonstandard mailbox sharing feature of JMAP for Mail, an
authenticated JMAP user with whom a mailbox had been shared could update the
permissions on that mailbox, including granting themselves or others further
access.  The correct behavior (now enforced) is to require administrative
access to the mailbox.


